- Rule 2: `DROP tcp --in-interface eth2` — drops all TCP transit
- Rule 3: `DROP udp --in-interface eth2` — drops all UDP transit (confirmed 15 hits, consistent with repeated RIP or other probes)
- Rule 4: `DROP icmp --in-interface eth2` — drops all ICMP transit 
